  "id": "Barking_&_Dagenham-26_00134_FULL",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "Change of use of the\r\ndwelling (Use Class C3) to a 3-bedroom HMO (Use Class C4) for up to four\r\noccupants",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;The proposed development results in the loss of a decent sized 3-bedroom family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that there&amp;nbsp;is an identified need, would cause a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers, and would not be located in an area with a high level of access to public transport.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;Additionally, the development site is not located within an area of high access to public transport and is therefore not considered an appropriate location for an HMO.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#x27;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&amp;nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)-&amp;nbsp;Policies&amp;nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&amp;nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)-&amp;nbsp;Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&amp;nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;The proposed development fails to demonstrate&amp;nbsp;that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229); font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;especially as the application site has a PTAL score of 0 indicating extremely poor access to public transport, and is within the&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;UP Controlled Parking Zone (CPZ)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229); font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;. The proposal is therefore likely to&amp;nbsp;exacerbate existing parking stress within the CPZ thus&amp;nbsp;add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;As such, it fails to comply with the following policies&amp;nbsp;which seek to ensure proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed and to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision:- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)-&amp;nbsp;Policies T1, T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)-&amp;nbsp;Policy DMT2 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;The proposed development would fail to provide sufficient internal space for both of the single bedrooms and would therefore provide a substandard quality of accommodation detrimental to the standard of living of future residents. Therefore, the proposal fails to comply with:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024), Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021) and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Policy&amp;nbsp;DMH5 (Houses in multiple occupation (HMOs)) of&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: rgb(229, 229, 229);&quot;&gt;the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan&amp;nbsp;(September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
